{"name":"Serendipity","hex":"#bde1d8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"serendipity","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The phenomenon of making an unplanned, fortunate discovery through a combination of unexpected circumstances and insightful recognition.","An unsought, unintended or unexpected, but fortunate, discovery or learning experience that occurs by accident."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serendipity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Serendipity","blocks":[{"text":"Serendipity is an unplanned fortunate discovery. The term was coined by Horace Walpole in 1754, after he read a Persian fairy tale called The Three Princes of Serendip, whose heroes constantly made lucky discoveries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Horace_Walpole.jpg/330px-Horace_Walpole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serendipity","wikidata":"Q166039"},{"title":"Serendipity (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Serendipity is a 2001 American romantic comedy film directed by Peter Chelsom, written by Marc Klein, and starring John Cusack and Kate Beckinsale. The film grossed $77.5 million on a $28 million budget."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a5/Serendipity_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serendipity_(film)","wikidata":"Q971468"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Post-it-note-white-bg.jpg/500px-Post-it-note-white-bg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Post-it-note-white-bg.jpg/500px-Post-it-note-white-bg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APost-it-note-white-bg.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wik